Z||000000||Philphine||11-13-2001||11:18 AM||||<BR>i was looking at the asg 5.0 page and noticed something. they show performance #'s up to 4900rpm like a stock 4.9, but under the chart there's a note. <P>it says their engine actualy makes more hp peaking at 6000rpm but the shift points of the stock tranny limit rpm to 4900.<P>i know there is going to be a lot of difference bettween a balanced/blueprinted engine and a decent pullout, but if i'm trying to use a manual tranny can i hope for a higher and useable redline too? i know my understanding of it is basic at best. i guess the computer has a hand in limiting it too?  a higher useable redline would make this engine that much more appealing.||||reg||1
