Z||000005||rockcrawl||11-13-2001||05:41 PM||||After you hear the sound the stock engine makes above ~5000 rpm, you won't want to do it very often. And there's no reason to, it won't get you anywhere. You'd be much better off shifting at 4500 and letting the torque take over. Top end improvements for this engine are coming, it's just a matter of time. For now we're stuck shifting at 4500.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mach10||11-13-2001||08:04 PM||||Do you like apples? Yes?<P>Well I'm going to start with a ground-up rebuild. Balance rotating assembly, blue-print etc. for the bottom end. <P>On the top, my rebuilder swears up and down that he can find stronger rockers/pushrods, stiffer springs, and better valves. Good-bye valve float and mushy top ends! Then it's off to the mill for a full pocket-port and polish. <P>Going to have to get creative with the ECM, though... My builder is suggesting using a camaro/firechicked ECM and some components... I'll see about that when I get there  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>How do you like THEM apples?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
